## SQ-POT-04 | accepted plants come back when the holder breaks
@group same run
@commands grep `PP-04`
@pass `PASS PP-04` for every `pot` holder: an accepted plant comes back when the holder breaks; `beautify:hanging_pot` rows carry `toggle: true` (the second click takes the plant back, the probe replants once) and drop the pot plus the plant
@fails `beautify:hanging_pot` drops only the pot without `toggle`: old probe copied (r1103 broke an empty pot after plant, take back, plant, take back); another holder eating the plant: new finding in flower_pots.md 3
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> pottest all
waitlog \[pottest\] INFO PP-DONE 900
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): floralench:large_pot drops the filled pot item with the plant kept inside it
# (flower_pots.md section 1 records that as its drop; large pots hidden since 2026-10-31), so its PP-04 FAIL line is
# accepted when every lost entry is one floralench:large_*_pot item; any other holder failing, or an empty drop, still fails
count \[pottest\] FAIL PP-04: (?!floralench:large_pot ) == 0
reject \[pottest\] FAIL PP-04: floralench:large_pot .*\[(?!1x floralench:large_\w+_pot\])[^\]]*\]
count \[pottest\] PASS PP-04: >= 1

## SQ-POT-04v | hand check: vanilla flower pot with Gossypium and IE hemp seed gives the plant back on a survival break
@group A
@commands Survival: place a flower pot, plant `miners_delight:gossypium`, break it by hand; same with `immersiveengineering:seed` (makes `immersiveengineering:potted_hemp`); also one explosion (`/summon tnt`) next to a third potted one
@pass Each break drops `minecraft:flower_pot` plus the plant (gossypium, or the IE hemp seed); the explosion drops what survives it, not air
@fails Nothing drops: the pack tables `kubejs/data/miners_delight/loot_tables/blocks/potted_gossypium.json` / `kubejs/data/immersiveengineering/loot_tables/blocks/potted_hemp.json` not loaded (`/reload`, check for a datapack error)
@from batches/r1102b/r_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> forceload add 288 496 296 508
sleep 3
> setblock 290 -60 500 minecraft:flower_pot
> setblock 292 -60 500 minecraft:flower_pot
> pbot spawn pot4 291 -60 504 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> clear pot4
> pbot hold pot4 miners_delight:gossypium
> pbot use pot4 290 -60 500 up
> pbot hold pot4 immersiveengineering:seed
> pbot use pot4 292 -60 500 up
> pbot remove pot4
> cdevtest state 290 -60 500
> cdevtest state 292 -60 500
> cdevtest break 290 -60 500 held=none
> cdevtest break 292 -60 500 held=none
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=break done= 30
count \[cdevtest\] verb=break .*broken=true >= 2
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
look the two `verb=state` lines: does each pot hold the plant (a potted_* id) or stay minecraft:flower_pot (refused, then nothing to lose)? A held plant must come back in the `verb=break drops=` line (flower_pot:1 plus the plant); flower_pot:1 alone on a filled pot = item loss. The explosion half of the row text is not automated

