## SQ-POT-10 | a flower pot used on a potted poppy makes the two-pot block; each half takes its own plant; break drops 2 pots and both plants
@group A
@commands a `minecraft:potted_poppy` at 880 -60 700 and an empty `minecraft:flower_pot` at 882 -60 700; `/cdevtest use` with `minecraft:flower_pot` (and once sneaking), with a dandelion on the tall half (hit 0.75,0.5,0.75), an empty hand on the short half (hit 0.25,0.4,0.25); `/cdevtest be`; `/cdevtest break`
@pass sneaking use leaves `minecraft:flower_pot` at 882; the plain use turns 880 into `creativecompat:double_flower_pot` with `PlantA:"minecraft:poppy"`; the dandelion goes in as `PlantB`; the empty hand takes the poppy back (main=poppy); break drops `minecraft:flower_pot:2` and the dandelion
@fails `DoublePot.onRightClickBlock` (event not reached: check `MinecraftForge.EVENT_BUS.register(DoublePot.class)` in CreativeCompat); `DoublePot.hitsPotB` (wrong half); loot table `creativecompat:blocks/double_flower_pot`; `DoublePotBlock.onRemove`
@reviewed 2026-11-22
> forceload add 860 680 900 720
> setblock 880 -60 700 minecraft:potted_poppy
> setblock 882 -60 700 minecraft:flower_pot
> cdevtest use 882 -60 700 held=minecraft:flower_pot face=up sneak
expect verb=use .*state=minecraft:flower_pot\b
> cdevtest use 880 -60 700 held=minecraft:flower_pot face=up
expect verb=use .*state=creativecompat:double_flower_pot
> cdevtest be 880 -60 700
expect verb=be .*PlantA:"minecraft:poppy"
> cdevtest use 880 -60 700 held=minecraft:dandelion face=up hit=0.75,0.5,0.75
> cdevtest be 880 -60 700
expect verb=be (?=.*PlantA:"minecraft:poppy")(?=.*PlantB:"minecraft:dandelion")
> cdevtest use 880 -60 700 held=air face=up hit=0.25,0.4,0.25
expect verb=use main=minecraft:poppy
> cdevtest break 880 -60 700
expect verb=break drops=(?=.*minecraft:flower_pot:2)(?=.*minecraft:dandelion:1)
look the be lines; the sneak use left 882 a plain empty flower pot; latest.log has no exception naming DoublePot

